          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+theory"} model theory
            %em definable closure
            of a subset of a model is a way of “generating a substructure” around that subset. The
            %em algebraic closure
            of a subset always contains the definable closure and generalizes the usual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+closure"} algebraic closure
            of fields.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math#mathml_76546a801fe813141a8a795bb51309c9f2e97435_1.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            be a small parameter set (i.e. a subset) of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monster+model"} monster model
            %math#mathml_76546a801fe813141a8a795bb51309c9f2e97435_2.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕄
                  %mo ⊧
                  %mi T
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{M} \models T.
            The
            %em definable closure
            %math#mathml_76546a801fe813141a8a795bb51309c9f2e97435_3.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} dcl
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{dcl}(A)
            of
            %math#mathml_76546a801fe813141a8a795bb51309c9f2e97435_4.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is the set of all tuples
            %math#mathml_76546a801fe813141a8a795bb51309c9f2e97435_5.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi 𝕄
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in \mathbb{M}
            such that there exists a formula
            %math#mathml_76546a801fe813141a8a795bb51309c9f2e97435_6.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi φ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi(x,y)
            and a tuple
            %math#mathml_76546a801fe813141a8a795bb51309c9f2e97435_7.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            from
            %math#mathml_76546a801fe813141a8a795bb51309c9f2e97435_8.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            such that
            %math#mathml_76546a801fe813141a8a795bb51309c9f2e97435_9.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            is the unique solution to
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_76546a801fe813141a8a795bb51309c9f2e97435_10.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi φ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi(a,y)
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_76546a801fe813141a8a795bb51309c9f2e97435_11.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi φ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕄
                      %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi(\mathbb{M}_x,y) = \{b\}
          %p
            To obtain the
            %em algebraic closure
            %math#mathml_76546a801fe813141a8a795bb51309c9f2e97435_12.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} acl
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{acl}(A)
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_76546a801fe813141a8a795bb51309c9f2e97435_13.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %h2#inside_a_monster Inside a monster
          %p
            Inside a sufficiently saturated and homogeneous model
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_76546a801fe813141a8a795bb51309c9f2e97435_14.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕄
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{M}
            %math#mathml_76546a801fe813141a8a795bb51309c9f2e97435_15.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            are definable over
            %math#mathml_76546a801fe813141a8a795bb51309c9f2e97435_16.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            if and only if they are fixed by the stabilizer
            %math#mathml_76546a801fe813141a8a795bb51309c9f2e97435_17.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝕄
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{Aut}(\mathbb{M}/A)
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_76546a801fe813141a8a795bb51309c9f2e97435_18.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math#mathml_76546a801fe813141a8a795bb51309c9f2e97435_19.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            if and only if they have finite orbit under
            %math#mathml_76546a801fe813141a8a795bb51309c9f2e97435_20.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝕄
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{Aut}(\mathbb{M}/A).
          %p
            %em Proof.
            To see nonobvious direction of the first claim, try the contrapositive: if every formula in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+%28in+model+theory%29"} type
            of
            %math#mathml_76546a801fe813141a8a795bb51309c9f2e97435_21.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            fails to uniquely pick out
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_76546a801fe813141a8a795bb51309c9f2e97435_22.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            %math#mathml_76546a801fe813141a8a795bb51309c9f2e97435_23.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b'
            which is not
            %math#mathml_76546a801fe813141a8a795bb51309c9f2e97435_24.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            but has the same type as
            %math#mathml_76546a801fe813141a8a795bb51309c9f2e97435_25.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b'
            is finitely consistent, therefore realized, and by homogeneity there is an automorphism interchanging
            %math#mathml_76546a801fe813141a8a795bb51309c9f2e97435_26.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_76546a801fe813141a8a795bb51309c9f2e97435_27.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b'
          %p
            To see the nonobvious direction of the second claim, try the contrapositive again: if
            %math#mathml_76546a801fe813141a8a795bb51309c9f2e97435_28.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            isn’t algebraic over
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_76546a801fe813141a8a795bb51309c9f2e97435_29.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math#mathml_76546a801fe813141a8a795bb51309c9f2e97435_30.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is infinite, in particular all conjunctions of finite fragments of its type. So we can iteratively obtain infinitely many disjoint realizations of its type, and again by homogeneity these must all lie in the same orbit.
            %math#mathml_76546a801fe813141a8a795bb51309c9f2e97435_31.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo □
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \square
          %p
            Saturation ensures that infinite definable sets become big—as big as the universe
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_76546a801fe813141a8a795bb51309c9f2e97435_32.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕄
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{M}
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                In
                = succeed "," do
                  %math#mathml_76546a801fe813141a8a795bb51309c9f2e97435_33.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                            %mi ACF
                          %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathsf{ACF}_p
                %math#mathml_76546a801fe813141a8a795bb51309c9f2e97435_34.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝕄
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{M}
                of a subset
                %math#mathml_76546a801fe813141a8a795bb51309c9f2e97435_35.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perfect+field"} perfect hull
                of
                = succeed "," do
                  %math#mathml_76546a801fe813141a8a795bb51309c9f2e97435_36.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔽
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}(A)
                %math#mathml_76546a801fe813141a8a795bb51309c9f2e97435_37.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔽
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}
                is
                %math#mathml_76546a801fe813141a8a795bb51309c9f2e97435_38.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℚ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
                for
                %math#mathml_76546a801fe813141a8a795bb51309c9f2e97435_39.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p = 0
                or the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+field"} prime field
                of the characteristic
                = succeed "," do
                  %math#mathml_76546a801fe813141a8a795bb51309c9f2e97435_40.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mi &gt;
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p &gt; 0
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separable+closure"} separable closure
            %li
              %p In the theory of an infinite set without structure, definable and algebraic closures coincide, and are trivial.
            %li
              %p
                In the relational structure consisting of the disjoint union of the cycle graphs of length
                %math#mathml_76546a801fe813141a8a795bb51309c9f2e97435_41.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                for each
                = succeed "," do
                  %math#mathml_76546a801fe813141a8a795bb51309c9f2e97435_42.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 1
                %math#mathml_76546a801fe813141a8a795bb51309c9f2e97435_43.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} dcl
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ∅
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{dcl}(\emptyset)
                is just the cycle graph of length
                = succeed "," do
                  %math#mathml_76546a801fe813141a8a795bb51309c9f2e97435_44.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
                %math#mathml_76546a801fe813141a8a795bb51309c9f2e97435_45.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} acl
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ∅
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{acl}(\emptyset)
                is the entire structure.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+%28in+model+theory%29"} type (in model theory)
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model-theoretic+Galois+theory"} model-theoretic Galois theory
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li
              Lou van den Dries,
              = succeed "." do
                %em An Introduction to Model-Theoretic Stability
            %li
              Dave Marker,
              = succeed "." do
                %em Model Theory: An Introduction
